<p>Every time I close the lid on my Mac or leave it on overnight, I have two angry apps hopping up and down in my Dock: my Cisco VPN and Microsoft Remote Desktop.</p>
<p>Last night: <code>defaults write com.apple.dock no-bouncing -bool TRUE; killall Dock</code></p>
<p>Bliss. Why doesn&rsquo;t macOS have an option to kill it in GUI?</p>
